{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall make the planks for the Mishkan.</b> Meaning, that the Mishkan is the name of the tent that is over the planks, and the planks are not called Mishkan but rather ״planks of the Mishkan.״" "<b>Planks of acacia wood, standing.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory in Yoma (72b) said that they stood in the direction of their growth. And it appears that they derived this precisely from the fact that He did not say in this manner, ״And you shall make the planks for the Mishkan, standing, of acacia wood,״ or ״And you shall make the planks of acacia wood for the Mishkan, standing״ — in which case it would have been understood that the standing is a requirement of the Mishkan, that they not lie on their sides. But by His saying <b>planks of acacia wood, standing,</b> He intimated that the word עֹמְדִים (standing) refers back also to the condition of the wood itself, that they should be in the order of their positioning during their growth." "<b>A mystical allusion:</b> the Mishkan — <b>planks (קְרָשִׁים)</b>; there is no קְרָשִׁים but rather קְשָׁרִים (bonds), for through its intermediary all aspects of holiness become bound and unified — supernal and lower — and all of them are alluded to within it. ״Ten cubits the length of a plank״ — there is no aspect of holiness that does not contain the totality of ten." "And His saying <b>and a cubit and a half</b> — here is an allusion to the unification of a whole makkah and a half makkah, which is the sod of ה (heh) and ד (dalet). Or it may intend the sod of the Yesod, Life of the Worlds, is the allusion of the cubit, and the crown of the Yesod is the aspect of half a cubit; you therefore find that each plank contains an allusion to the ten that exist within every sefirah, and they also contain an allusion to Tzaddik and Tzedek unified in the breadth." "The number of the planks is forty-eight, and this is the sod of (Isaiah 54:12) ״And I will make your windows of kadkod.״" "Their name, אֲדָנִים, declares, and their construction justifies their spiritual dimension — for they are the aspect of the Shekhinah, which is called by the name Adonai, and which receives the foundation within her. And their number is one hundred, and this is the sod of 'the small one reaches one hundred'; she is also the tenth of the levels and encompasses all the tenths — behold, one hundred."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:51.967088889Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}